IN <TERMIOS.H>

Normally:
User types: h e l l o
Program receives nothing
until Enter is pressed.
This is called canonical mode.

When you disable it:
User types: h
Program instantly receives h
User types: e
Program instantly receives e
No need to press Enter.

We'll restore these settings, & trun the canonical mode ON, because without that terminal remains broken after program exits. 

# WHY USE WRITE & NOT COUT ? IN THIS LIBRARY ? 
Ans -> No hard constraint, Most of the time you'll see no difference, but for terminal editors and shells, people prefer the lower-level API because it gives precise control.